From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 15:22:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] addons: enable IPTV Simple and FFmpegDirect on first start

The kodi-pvr-iptvsimple and kodi-inputstream-ffmpegdirect packages
install pvr.iptvsimple and inputstream.ffmpegdirect next to Kodi's own
add-ons, and Kodi registers an add-on it finds for the first time as
disabled unless the add-on manifest names it. A fresh installation came
up without Live TV, and the PVR client showed up nowhere in the menus
until it was enabled from the add-on browser. Listing both as optional
system add-ons enables them on first start and leaves the user free to
disable them; on an installation without the packages the entries have
no effect.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 system/addon-manifest.xml | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/system/addon-manifest.xml
+++ b/system/addon-manifest.xml
@@ -56,7 +56,9 @@
   <addon>xbmc.webinterface</addon>
   <addon optional="true">game.shader.presets</addon>
   <addon optional="true">inputstream.adaptive</addon>
+  <addon optional="true">inputstream.ffmpegdirect</addon>
   <addon optional="true">peripheral.joystick</addon>
+  <addon optional="true">pvr.iptvsimple</addon>
   <addon optional="true">repository.dangowrt.webapps</addon>
   <addon optional="true">service.xbmc.versioncheck</addon>
 </addons>
